# Production build overlay.
#
# Applied on top of sdkconfig.defaults to produce a PRODUCTION image:
#
#   idf.py -B build_production \
#          -DSDKCONFIG=sdkconfig.production \
#          -DSDKCONFIG_DEFAULTS="sdkconfig.defaults;sdkconfig.production.defaults" \
#          build
#
# Turning ARGUS_DIAGNOSTIC_MODE off does two things that must stay in step:
#   - app_main does not create the diagnostic task (16 KB of heap) and does
#     not compile the diagnostic menu or the test headers;
#   - main/CMakeLists.txt excludes every argus_tests_*.c translation unit
#     from the link, so the fixtures (~9 KB of .bss, including a duplicate
#     6,952-byte topic table) are absent from the image rather than merely
#     unreachable.
#
# The diagnostic build remains the default (sdkconfig.defaults) and is what
# acceptance testing runs on COM5. This overlay exists so the production
# image can be built and its exclusions PROVEN, not asserted.
#
# Deliberately contains no credentials. Wi-Fi passphrase and machine secret
# are set through menuconfig into the gitignored sdkconfig and are never
# committed.
CONFIG_ARGUS_DIAGNOSTIC_MODE=n
